  "python_conversion_notes": "Requires reverse-engineering CSignalUniversal.mqh and TrailingUniversal.mqh to extract the 8 pattern signal models and trailing logic. The CExpert framework handles position management, signal aggregation, and order execution internally - all of which must be reimplemented. The threshold-based voting system (patterns contribute weighted votes, compared against open/close thresholds) is the core mechanism. SL/TP are in points (not pips) and may need digit-adjustment logic for 5-digit brokers. The Signal_PriceLevel=0.0 means market execution at current price. Pending order expiration of 4 bars needs bar-counting logic. CMoneyFixedLot uses a fixed lot size with a percent risk parameter that likely serves as a maximum margin limit.",
